:stop_sign: **Crash Risk**: `len(audit_evidence)` raises `TypeError` if `audit_evidence` is a `Mapping` that does not implement `__len__` (e.g., a custom `Mapping` subclass or `collections.abc.Mapping` without `__len__`). The parameter type annotation only promises `Mapping[str, Any]`, but `Mapping` does not require `Sized`. Replace the length check with an explicit `not audit_evidence` or `not dict(audit_evidence)` to safely handle any conforming `Mapping`.
```suggestion
        if capture_decision_evidence_enabled(self._snapshot) and (
            not isinstance(audit_evidence, Mapping) or not audit_evidence
        ):
```
